/-!
# The coefficient field on a closed cube is a local observable

The local information carried by a region is generated by the integrals of the
entries of the coefficient field against test functions supported in that
region.  It is therefore an integral notion, while the solution of a Dirichlet
problem on the cube is built from the *field* on the cube, an element of the
Banach space of continuous matrix fields on the closed cube.  This module
bridges the two.

Two elementary steps do it.  First, the value of a continuous field at a point
is the limit of its averages over closed balls shrinking to that point, and each
such average is a scalar multiple of the integral of an entry against the
indicator of the ball, hence a local observable as soon as the ball lies in the
region.  Second, a map into the continuous fields on a compact carrier is Borel
measurable as soon as its values at the points of a countable dense subset of
the carrier are measurable: the distance to a fixed field is the supremum of the
pointwise distances over that subset, so the preimage of every closed ball is
measurable, and in a separable metric space the closed balls generate the Borel
sets.

Applied to `y + □_n` the two steps give the conclusion for the local
information of the *closed* cube itself: the points of the open cube are dense
in the closed cube, and around each of them a closed ball still fits inside the
cube, so no enlargement of the region is needed.

## Main results

* `closedCubeAt_subset_closure_cubeSetAt` — the closed cube is the closure of the
  open cube.
* `measurable_coefficientCutoff_apply_local` — the value of the coefficient field
  at a point interior to the region is a local observable.
* `measurable_coefficientCutoffRestrict_local` — the coefficient field on the
  closed cube is a local observable of the closed cube.

## References

* ABK26, the cutoff coefficient field of Section 3 and the localized Dirichlet
  problems of Section 5.1.
-/

namespace Algsuperdiff.Section5.Support

